 "notes": [
  "Objects are Analog, Binary and Multi-state Values only. Rows without a read-only mark in the manual are listed as writable.",
  "Temperature objects use °F or °C depending on the INMODE (sensor type/mode) setting.",
  "Start-up settings can be read but not written over BACnet; Heat-Timer says to set them at the panel first.",
  "The manual prints some rows as ranges (BSTATUS = 300-331 (one name printed for the whole range); COMERR00-31 = 600-631; LOCK00-31 = 1500-1531; MODE00-31 = 2000-2031; SCHEDULES00-55 = 3400-3455). Only the first and last printed objects of each range are listed here; the ones in between follow the same pattern.",
  "Per-boiler objects come in blocks of 32 (00-31); the Lead Boiler coding depends on Boiler Type (table on manual page 11).",
  "Variable list: manual pages 10-11."
 ],
 "integration": {
  "summary": "The HWRQ sequences up to 32 boiler stages from its own outdoor reset or setpoint. From the BMS, read the calculated target, system and outdoor temperatures, boiler status and lockouts; adjust the setpoint/offset, put individual boilers in Auto/Standby/Off/On with MODE, and force a day/night shift if needed.",
